{
  "info": {
    "name": "Integriq — endpoint response cache and problem documents (gateway-response-cache-and-problem-errors)",
    "description": "Newman test of openspec/changes/archive/2026-11-25-gateway-response-cache-and-problem-errors.\n\n- REQ-RCPE-001: an endpoint caching GET answers for 60 seconds answers the same question twice with one call to the source; the first answer carries `X-Cache: MISS`, the second `X-Cache: HIT`, and the call log marks the hit. Clear cache on the endpoint (`POST /api/endpoints/{id}/cache/clear`) makes the next call reach the source again; clearing needs a signed-in user with the right and an existing endpoint.\n- REQ-RCPE-002: a gateway error is a problem document: a wrong key gets 401 with content type `application/problem+json`, a `type` URI for authentication failures and the old `error` member; a path no endpoint serves gets a problem document too.\n\nThe source is the instance's own `status.php` (location `base_url`, upstream path `/status.php`), so nothing outside the instance is needed. The cache lives in the distributed cache: on an instance without one (no Redis or Memcached) nothing is kept between requests and the HIT checks are reported as skipped, not passed. Setup creates a source, a cached endpoint, an API key rule and a protected endpoint through OpenRegister; teardown deletes them.\n\nSPDX-License-Identifier: EUPL-1.2\nSPDX-FileCopyrightText: 2026 Conduction B.V. <info@conduction.nl>",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
